1
00:06:02,239 --> 00:06:06,847
The less money you have in this tax bag the less tax you have to pay

2
00:06:07,103 --> 00:06:09,151
But you still have to pay tax

3
00:06:09,407 --> 00:06:11,199
On, for example, share fund account

4
00:06:11,455 --> 00:06:16,319
Then it is true that then you can offset your losses against your winnings but you can't do that in an investment savings account

5
00:06:16,575 --> 00:06:17,343
That is a disadvantage

6
00:06:17,599 --> 00:06:19,135
A little premium though

7
00:06:19,647 --> 00:06:21,951
You cannot shiny shares in an investment savings account

8
00:06:23,231 --> 00:06:25,535
And most people don't do it so it doesn't matter

9
00:06:26,047 --> 00:06:29,119
Some securities you cannot have on an investment savings account

10
00:06:29,375 --> 00:06:31,935
For example, unlisted

11
00:06:32,191 --> 00:06:36,287
Shares not on the stock exchange if you were to buy some shares in an unlisted company
